  {
    "sha": "b89eabbb6b41d1e9d71961588937ae9d6c2052b5",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVouz_toAKGI4OWVhYmJiNmI0MWQxZTlkNzE5NjE1ODg5MzdhZTlkNmMyMDUyYjU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T09:37:38Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T09:37:38Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(thread): hold the thread grant to the model's own wall, not the declared circle\n\nPR #1099 review: the solid-law grant recognised a hole's minor wall with\nthe drill rim's band (max(2 % r, 0.1 mm)) but capped the cutter at the\nDECLARED major circle, so a declared hole up to that band wider than, or\noff the centre of, the model's hole overcut its thread silently.\n\nThe band now only recognises the wall; the cap is the hit facet's own\nradius about the axis (its nearest on-circle vertex) plus the thread\ndepth plus the allowance. major_rims grows a through hole's major circle\nfrom the model's own rim loop when that stands nearer than the declared\none.\n\nPinned by thread_mill_rim:\na_declared_hole_wider_than_the_models_by_a_hair_convicts,\na_declared_hole_off_the_models_centre_by_a_hair_convicts (the reviewer's\ncases, blind and through) and\na_matched_thread_stays_clean_at_other_sizes_and_through.\n\nFixes #1071\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
