  {
    "sha": "ea76d5df03d6fc3fdc8a6c76c02edda39eb1f300",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVouz_toAKGVhNzZkNWRmMDNkNmZjM2ZkYzhhNmM3NmMwMmVkZGEzOWViMWYzMDA",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T13:58:35Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T13:58:35Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(thread): grade a thread's wall at the facet's nearest point, not its corners\n\nReview of 434a464a: a flat or chord wall whose corners stand on the\ndeclared circle was read as the bore's wall and graded at its nearest\nvertex. A D-bore's flat (1 mm in), an octagon's sides (0.38 mm in) and a\n16-gon's were cut through with no warning.\n\nThe solid-law grant (thread_bore::wall_radius, the wall and mouth\nbranches) and major_rims now measure the facet's or loop's nearest point\nto the bore axis. That point must itself be on the band for the facet to\ncount as the thread's material. The wall stands there, credited at most\nCHORD_CREDIT (DEV_TOL, 0.01 mm) toward its nearest vertex. The credit is\ntessellation of a round hole, which the STEP importer meshes at half\nthat; never a flat.\n\nmajor_rims, thread_bores and loop_nearest move to\noperation/thread_rims.rs, so material_source.rs stays at 350 lines.\n\nNew pins:\n- thread_mill_rim: a_flat_whose_corners_stand_on_the_circle_convicts\n  (it failed on 434a464a: D-bore, no warning) and\n  a_fine_polygon_bore_still_verifies_clean.\n- thread_bore unit tests.\n\nRefs #1071\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
